## 18. Common interview mistakes to avoid

-   Saying round robin guarantees equal CPU usage.
-   Treating active connections as a perfect measure of workload.
-   Assuming two load-balancer instances automatically provide HA.
-   Claiming that Nginx Open Source supports every NGINX Plus feature.
-   Treating `proxy_read_timeout` as a total request deadline.
-   Retrying every request without considering duplicate side effects.
-   Using average latency alone.
-   Declaring capacity based on a short test without SLOs or failure
    testing.
-   Assuming a 502 or 504 proves a particular root cause.
-   Removing a backend without checking whether the survivors have
    enough capacity.
-   Increasing timeouts without considering queueing and resource
    exhaustion.
-   Treating health checks as a substitute for monitoring and incident
    response.

