## Final interview takeaway

A strong answer does more than name an algorithm. It explains **why the
design fits the workload, what happens when components fail, how the
team measures performance, how much traffic the system can safely
sustain, and how recovery is verified in production**.

For a senior engineer, demonstrate technical reasoning and
evidence-based troubleshooting. For an engineering leader, additionally
demonstrate ownership of reliability objectives, capacity risk,
operational readiness, incident communication, and measurable outcomes.
